WEBVTT

00:00.849 --> 00:01.949
&lt;i>Previously on...&lt;/i>

00:02.877 --> 00:04.677
Tonight would be&lt;br/>a great time

00:04.679 --> 00:06.913
to tell Larry that you're&lt;br/>not Jeff Strongman,

00:06.915 --> 00:08.147
that you're really&lt;br/>Alan Harper.

00:08.149 --> 00:10.349
If you tell Larry&lt;br/>who you really are,

00:10.351 --> 00:12.952
then he's gonna wonder&lt;br/>why &lt;i>I&lt;/i> didn't tell him.

00:12.954 --> 00:17.223
Will you do me the honor&lt;br/>of becoming Mrs. Alan Harper?

00:17.858 --> 00:19.225
Who the hell&lt;br/>is Alan Harper?

00:19.227 --> 00:22.495
Larry! Look! Boobs!

00:22.497 --> 00:24.497
♪ &lt;i>Men.&lt;/i> ♪

00:24.499 --> 00:27.667
We can go in the other room and&lt;br/>you can play with them. Huh?

00:27.669 --> 00:29.709
Really?&lt;br/>In the middle of the day?

00:29.734 --> 00:31.170
Mm-hmm.

00:31.171 --> 00:33.272
Wait a minute.&lt;br/>Who's Alan Harper?

00:33.274 --> 00:35.942
Uh, I am gonna answer that,&lt;br/>but before I do...

00:35.944 --> 00:37.677
What do you say, Gretchie?

00:37.679 --> 00:39.112
Will you marry me?

00:39.114 --> 00:40.580
Yes.

00:40.582 --> 00:42.915
Oh, my God!

00:45.052 --> 00:48.054
You've made me the-the&lt;br/>happiest man in the world.

00:48.056 --> 00:50.022
Don't cry. Don't cry.&lt;br/>Don't cry.

00:50.024 --> 00:52.792
A-And for your&lt;br/>question, Larry,

00:52.794 --> 00:55.962
I just want to say that&lt;br/>everything you've known about me

00:55.964 --> 00:57.363
is a lie.

00:57.365 --> 00:59.198
My real name is Alan.

00:59.200 --> 01:01.901
That's okay.&lt;br/>My real name is Lawrence.

01:01.903 --> 01:04.804
All right, this is gonna be&lt;br/>a lot harder than I thought.

01:04.806 --> 01:06.672
Um, uh, Lyndsey

01:06.674 --> 01:08.875
is my ex-girlfriend.&lt;br/>When you and she

01:08.877 --> 01:10.610
got together,&lt;br/>I made up a fake name

01:10.612 --> 01:12.879
so that I could meet you&lt;br/>and stay close to Lyndsey.

01:12.881 --> 01:14.847
But then it turns out&lt;br/>I actually like you

01:14.849 --> 01:16.282
more than I like Lyndsey.

01:16.284 --> 01:18.851
I like you&lt;br/>more than Lyndsey, too!

01:20.120 --> 01:22.155
What the hell&lt;br/>is happening here?!

01:23.624 --> 01:25.558
So your name's&lt;br/>not really Jeff Strongman,

01:25.560 --> 01:27.994
it's Alan Harper,&lt;br/>and you used to date Lyndsey?

01:27.996 --> 01:29.362
For four years.

01:29.364 --> 01:31.330
Did you know about this?

01:32.800 --> 01:34.967
Yes. He was my boyfriend.

01:34.969 --> 01:38.037
But-but I'm with &lt;i>you&lt;/i> now,&lt;br/>and only you.

01:38.039 --> 01:39.272
A-And I'm really, really sorry.

01:39.274 --> 01:42.275
Oh, save it, Jeff--&lt;br/>if that's even your real name.

01:42.277 --> 01:44.844
I think I made it pretty clear&lt;br/>it's not, but o-okay.

01:44.846 --> 01:47.680
I told Alan that I thought&lt;br/>he should tell you the truth,

01:47.682 --> 01:49.382
because I thought&lt;br/>you deserved to know.

01:49.384 --> 01:51.017
How could you keep this from me?

01:51.019 --> 01:53.252
I would never lie to you.&lt;br/>This is unbelievable!

01:53.254 --> 01:55.288
I never wanted&lt;br/>any of this to happen.

01:55.290 --> 01:58.324
Well, it did-- and now&lt;br/>I've lost my two best friends.

01:58.326 --> 02:01.394
And this time I'm not&lt;br/>talking about your boobs.

02:01.396 --> 02:03.996
I don't want to see&lt;br/>either one of you again.

02:03.998 --> 02:06.265
And I'm still not talking&lt;br/>about your boobs!

02:06.267 --> 02:07.900
The wedding's off!

02:07.902 --> 02:09.302
Larry, wait!

02:09.304 --> 02:10.670
Oh, God, see?

02:10.672 --> 02:13.039
This is exactly why&lt;br/>I didn't want to tell him.

02:13.041 --> 02:15.107
Now both Lyndsey&lt;br/>&lt;i>and&lt;/i> Larry hate me,

02:15.109 --> 02:17.610
and I've ruined the lives&lt;br/>of two wonderful people.

02:17.612 --> 02:20.680
I'll never forget&lt;br/>the look on-- ooh, boobs.

02:20.682 --> 02:23.049
♪ Men, men, men, men, manly men,&lt;br/>men, men ♪

02:23.051 --> 02:26.221
♪ Ah.&lt;br/>♪ Men.

02:26.226 --> 02:30.226
&lt;font color="#00FF00">♪ Two and a Half Men 11x22 ♪&lt;/font>&lt;br/>&lt;font color="#00FFFF">Oh WALD-E, Good Times Ahead&lt;/font>&lt;br/>Original Air Date on

02:28.227 --> 02:30.227
== sync, corrected by &lt;font color=#00FF00>elderman&lt;/font> ==&lt;br/>&lt;font color=#00FFFF>@elder_man&lt;/font>

02:28.753 --> 02:30.086
♪ &lt;i>Men.&lt;/i> ♪

02:30.088 --> 02:33.089
Say hello to my little friend.

02:33.091 --> 02:34.291
What is &lt;i>that?&lt;/i>

02:34.293 --> 02:36.393
This is the most advanced

02:36.395 --> 02:39.262
robotic artificial&lt;br/>intelligence today.

02:39.264 --> 02:40.730
I call him WALD-E.

02:40.732 --> 02:41.798
Get it?

02:41.800 --> 02:42.966
'Cause I'm Walden,

02:42.968 --> 02:44.334
and the movie &lt;i>WALL-E?&lt;/i>

02:44.336 --> 02:45.969
WALD-E?

02:46.804 --> 02:48.538
Say hello to my friend Jenny.

02:48.540 --> 02:51.541
Hello to my friend Jenny.

02:51.543 --> 02:53.677
I programmed him to be funny.

02:53.679 --> 02:55.612
I beg to differ.

02:55.614 --> 02:57.247
You're just jealous&lt;br/>'cause you don't have

02:57.249 --> 02:58.748
an electronic friend&lt;br/>to play with.

02:58.750 --> 03:00.650
Trust me, I have a whole drawer

03:00.652 --> 03:02.819
of electronic friends&lt;br/>I can play with.

03:02.821 --> 03:07.190
Then maybe we can have&lt;br/>a zero-one-one-way.

03:07.192 --> 03:09.993
That's a three-way in binary.

03:09.995 --> 03:13.530
Oh, WALD-E, good times ahead.

03:13.532 --> 03:14.898
Hey.

03:14.900 --> 03:16.933
Oh. Hey, check out&lt;br/>my new robot.

03:16.935 --> 03:20.470
I detect no sign&lt;br/>of intelligent life.

03:20.472 --> 03:23.139
I'm not in the mood for this.&lt;br/>Can you turn him off?

03:23.141 --> 03:25.508
Can you turn &lt;i>him&lt;/i> off?

03:26.544 --> 03:29.346
I wish I could, WALD-E,&lt;br/>I wish I could.

03:30.615 --> 03:32.282
What's going on?&lt;br/>Larry just texted me.

03:32.284 --> 03:34.484
He wants to see me.&lt;br/>What do you think he wants?

03:34.486 --> 03:35.552
Well,

03:35.554 --> 03:37.854
given the fact&lt;br/>you blew up his entire life,

03:37.856 --> 03:39.990
I'm guessing he&lt;br/>either wants to kick your ass,

03:39.992 --> 03:43.827
&lt;i>or&lt;/i> rip your face off so you&lt;br/>can &lt;i>watch&lt;/i> him kick your ass.

03:43.829 --> 03:45.929
Oh, this is all my fault.

03:45.931 --> 03:47.430
I should have just been honest

03:47.432 --> 03:48.802
and told the truth&lt;br/>right from the start--

03:48.803 --> 03:50.410
lying is&lt;br/>never the answer.

03:50.869 --> 03:52.602
Ooh, I know,&lt;br/>I'll tell him I'm sick.

03:52.604 --> 03:54.371
What's a trendy illness?

03:54.373 --> 03:55.805
Alan, you have to man up

03:55.807 --> 03:57.807
and face the consequences&lt;br/>of your actions.

03:57.809 --> 03:59.109
Maybe you're right.

03:59.111 --> 04:00.910
I at least owe him that much.

04:00.912 --> 04:03.346
I'll just go and... Hah-choo!

04:03.348 --> 04:05.749
Oh! Oh. Oh.

04:05.751 --> 04:06.983
Alan?&lt;br/>Mm-hmm?

04:06.985 --> 04:09.486
When people sneeze,&lt;br/>they don't say, "Hah-choo,

04:09.488 --> 04:11.221
oh, ew, ooh."

04:11.223 --> 04:12.389
Okay, fine.

04:12.391 --> 04:14.791
But when he beats me&lt;br/>within an inch of my life,

04:14.793 --> 04:16.192
you're on bedpan duty.

04:16.194 --> 04:18.995
Okay, if it makes you&lt;br/>feel better, I'll come with you.

04:18.997 --> 04:21.898
He only wants to&lt;br/>go so when Larry beats you up,

04:21.900 --> 04:23.566
he can say, "I told you so."

04:23.568 --> 04:25.568
That is not true.

04:25.570 --> 04:26.703
Even though&lt;br/>I repeatedly

04:26.705 --> 04:29.506
told him to stop lying&lt;br/>about who he was,

04:29.508 --> 04:31.941
and deceiving the people&lt;br/>around him,

04:31.943 --> 04:34.344
and eventually it&lt;br/>would blow up in his face,

04:34.346 --> 04:37.347
I'm not going to say,&lt;br/>"I told you so."

04:37.349 --> 04:38.515
Well, I appreciate that.

04:38.517 --> 04:40.750
I want to film Larry&lt;br/>kicking his ass

04:40.752 --> 04:43.320
and then say,&lt;br/>"I told you so""

04:43.322 --> 04:44.888
♪ &lt;i>Men.&lt;/i> ♪

04:44.890 --> 04:46.189
Hey, Alan.

04:46.191 --> 04:48.258
Oh, hey,&lt;br/>hey, Larry!

04:53.497 --> 04:55.031
I don't have a weapon.

04:55.033 --> 04:56.366
Hi. I'm Walden,

04:56.368 --> 04:57.634
Alan's friend.

04:57.636 --> 04:59.402
Uh, just act like I'm not here,

04:59.404 --> 05:01.504
and punch like&lt;br/>no one's watchin'.

05:01.506 --> 05:03.473
And...

05:03.475 --> 05:04.307
action.

05:04.309 --> 05:05.542
So, you, uh, you said

05:05.544 --> 05:06.576
you wanted to talk?

05:06.578 --> 05:08.345
No, no, no, louder.

05:08.347 --> 05:09.479
I'm sorry. What?

05:09.481 --> 05:11.881
Louder. There's a lot&lt;br/>of ambient noise in here.

05:11.883 --> 05:14.351
So, so, you&lt;br/>said you wanted to talk?

05:14.353 --> 05:17.754
Yeah, I actually came here&lt;br/>to tell you that I forgive you!

05:17.756 --> 05:19.089
No! Cut! Cut!

05:19.091 --> 05:21.191
What's... Wait, wait,&lt;br/>you &lt;i>forgive&lt;/i> him?

05:21.193 --> 05:22.859
Yeah, I realized&lt;br/>all this anger isn't good.

05:22.861 --> 05:24.260
I had to let it all go.

05:24.262 --> 05:26.329
No!

05:26.331 --> 05:27.931
He's not gonna&lt;br/>learn his lesson

05:27.933 --> 05:29.966
if you forgive him.&lt;br/>The only way he's gonna learn

05:29.968 --> 05:32.369
a lesson is&lt;br/>through pain and suffering

05:32.371 --> 05:34.371
and possibly losing a tooth.

05:34.373 --> 05:36.573
No, no. He's gonna be&lt;br/>my brother-in-law

05:36.575 --> 05:38.641
and make an honest woman&lt;br/>out of Gretchen.

05:38.643 --> 05:41.945
She's not gonna be an&lt;br/>honest woman on our wedding night.

05:41.947 --> 05:44.681
That's the guy I know and love&lt;br/>who's banging my sister.

05:44.683 --> 05:46.783
I do love banging&lt;br/>your sister.

05:48.153 --> 05:51.521
No, the only banging I want&lt;br/>to see is you banging his face!

05:51.523 --> 05:52.622
Oh,

05:52.624 --> 05:54.858
that didn't come out right.

05:54.860 --> 05:57.427
Gretchen is the most amazing&lt;br/>woman I've ever met.

05:57.429 --> 05:59.963
I-I just have to scrape together&lt;br/>enough money for the wedding.

05:59.965 --> 06:02.065
Oh, I know what you mean--&lt;br/>mine and Lyndsey's

06:02.067 --> 06:03.500
was costing me a fortune.

06:03.502 --> 06:06.202
I already paid for the flowers,&lt;br/>the cake, the tux.

06:06.204 --> 06:08.571
Too bad you can't&lt;br/>just take &lt;i>his&lt;/i> wedding.

06:08.573 --> 06:11.341
Or can I?

06:11.343 --> 06:12.675
I was kidding.

06:12.677 --> 06:15.412
Well, why not? I mean,&lt;br/>this cup says "Peter" on it,

06:15.414 --> 06:17.814
but Peter&lt;br/>wasn't there to get it.

06:19.316 --> 06:21.351
I'm not gonna use it.&lt;br/>Me and Lyndsey are through,

06:21.353 --> 06:22.485
so you might as well.

06:22.487 --> 06:24.287
You can't mooch a wedding

06:24.289 --> 06:26.456
that you just destroyed.

06:26.458 --> 06:28.358
I know. How great is that?

06:28.360 --> 06:30.193
Classic Alan Harper.

06:30.195 --> 06:32.126
Jeff Strongman.&lt;br/>Mm.

06:32.127 --> 06:34.127
I don't know how&lt;br/>I didn't see through it sooner.

06:34.266 --> 06:36.299
It's such&lt;br/>an obviously made-up name.

06:36.301 --> 06:38.201
Yeah.&lt;br/>Jeff.

06:40.271 --> 06:42.172
♪ &lt;i>Men.&lt;/i> ♪

06:42.674 --> 06:45.875
Mom, this is my fiancée,&lt;br/>Gretchen Martin.

06:45.877 --> 06:48.577
It is so nice to finally&lt;br/>meet you, Evelyn.

06:48.579 --> 06:50.713
Oh, you, too, dear.

06:50.715 --> 06:52.648
How far along &lt;i>are&lt;/i> you?

06:52.650 --> 06:54.617
What?&lt;br/>Uh, my mother assumes that

06:54.619 --> 06:57.086
since you agreed to marry me,&lt;br/>you must be pregnant.

06:57.088 --> 06:58.754
No, I'm not pregnant.

06:58.756 --> 07:01.123
Are you after my money?&lt;br/>Of course not.

07:01.125 --> 07:04.527
&lt;i>¿Estas buscando trabajo&lt;/i>&lt;br/>&lt;i>en el mundo nuevo?&lt;/i>

07:04.529 --> 07:05.828
What?

07:05.830 --> 07:07.930
Not looking&lt;br/>for a green card, either.

07:08.732 --> 07:10.967
You must genuinely like Alan.&lt;br/>Yeah.

07:10.969 --> 07:13.536
This is uncharted&lt;br/>territory for me.

07:13.538 --> 07:15.504
I know. She actually&lt;br/>loves me for me.

07:15.506 --> 07:17.873
I mean, I had to pretend&lt;br/>to be another person

07:17.875 --> 07:19.508
to make it all&lt;br/>happen, but still.

07:19.510 --> 07:22.011
Oh, that is &lt;i>some&lt;/i> ring&lt;br/>you bought her.

07:22.013 --> 07:24.447
Oh, actually, that's the ring&lt;br/>my ex-husband got me.

07:24.449 --> 07:28.150
But I still had it-- I figured&lt;br/>why make Alan buy another one?

07:28.152 --> 07:30.286
My God, you've&lt;br/>found your soul mate.

07:30.288 --> 07:33.089
I know. Our honeymoon is&lt;br/>at her cousin's time-share.

07:33.091 --> 07:35.725
He can't use it, 'cause&lt;br/>he had a heart attack.

07:35.727 --> 07:37.493
We're so blessed.

07:37.495 --> 07:39.428
Speaking of blessings,

07:39.430 --> 07:42.298
I just want to thank you&lt;br/>for raising such a caring,

07:42.300 --> 07:44.600
thoughtful,&lt;br/>intelligent son.

07:46.637 --> 07:48.504
Oh, you're serious.

07:49.973 --> 07:51.574
So, when's the big day?

07:51.576 --> 07:53.109
Oh, uh, it's&lt;br/>next Saturday.

07:53.111 --> 07:56.012
We're just gonna have a small&lt;br/>affair here at the house.

07:56.014 --> 07:57.880
We're trying to&lt;br/>keep costs down.

07:57.882 --> 07:59.148
Are your parents coming?

07:59.150 --> 08:01.050
Oh, no, my parents&lt;br/>have passed away.

08:01.052 --> 08:03.652
Again, we're&lt;br/>so blessed.

08:04.788 --> 08:07.323
So, where are you planning&lt;br/>on living after you marry?

08:07.325 --> 08:09.158
Oh, we're not in a rush&lt;br/>to go anywhere.

08:09.160 --> 08:11.127
I mean, beach house, no rent...

08:12.262 --> 08:14.797
Don't be ridiculous--&lt;br/>you need your own place.

08:14.799 --> 08:16.932
Well, that's easier&lt;br/>said than done, Mom.

08:16.934 --> 08:20.202
How about for your wedding&lt;br/>if I give you a down payment

08:20.204 --> 08:23.439
towards your own...&lt;br/>Oh, I love you, Mom!

08:25.208 --> 08:28.010
I won't go &lt;i>that&lt;/i> far,&lt;br/>but thank you.

08:28.012 --> 08:29.845
♪ &lt;i>Men.&lt;/i> ♪

08:33.950 --> 08:35.317
Walden.

08:35.319 --> 08:37.453
Oh, don't worry,&lt;br/>Alan's not with me.

08:37.455 --> 08:38.921
Wow, it's amazing

08:38.923 --> 08:41.257
how infrequently&lt;br/>I actually get to say that.

08:41.259 --> 08:42.792
What's up?

08:42.794 --> 08:46.062
I just wanted&lt;br/>to make sure you're okay.

08:46.064 --> 08:47.830
That's sweet, but I'm fine.

08:47.832 --> 08:50.766
When I get dumped, I usually&lt;br/>end up sobbing in a bathtub,

08:50.768 --> 08:52.435
listening to Michael Bublé.

08:52.437 --> 08:54.904
I call it my "Bublé bath."

08:55.705 --> 08:57.973
You sure you're all right?&lt;br/>Yeah.

08:57.975 --> 08:59.542
I was about to marry Larry,

08:59.544 --> 09:01.577
a guy who once called&lt;br/>venetian blind cleaners

09:01.579 --> 09:03.846
because he wanted to help&lt;br/>handicapped Italians.

09:03.848 --> 09:05.314
Look, if Alan

09:05.316 --> 09:07.316
and Gretchen are supposed&lt;br/>to be together,

09:07.318 --> 09:08.951
I wish them the best.

09:08.953 --> 09:12.354
If you need anything,&lt;br/>don't hesitate to call me.

09:12.356 --> 09:14.023
Thanks.&lt;br/>Okay.

09:19.530 --> 09:23.566
Siri, remind me to draw&lt;br/>a Bublé bath tonight.

09:26.937 --> 09:29.138
Mm, what's that, Larry?

09:29.140 --> 09:33.242
You forgive me&lt;br/>and you still want to marry me?

09:33.244 --> 09:34.944
Oh, Alan...

09:34.946 --> 09:38.714
you never stopped loving me&lt;br/>and you want to marry me, too?

09:39.883 --> 09:42.852
I am the luckiest woman&lt;br/>in the world.

09:52.763 --> 09:55.131
♪ &lt;i>Men.&lt;/i> ♪

09:57.004 --> 09:59.038
♪ &lt;i>Men.&lt;/i> ♪

09:59.040 --> 10:01.074
Everybody, freeze.

10:01.076 --> 10:02.642
What the hell?

10:02.644 --> 10:05.645
Berta, I know&lt;br/>where you hide your pot.

10:07.081 --> 10:09.015
WALD-E!

10:09.017 --> 10:10.550
No...!

10:10.552 --> 10:13.720
Now, &lt;i>that's&lt;/i> how you deal&lt;br/>with a DEA drone.

10:13.722 --> 10:15.188
No!

10:15.190 --> 10:16.923
It's my robot!

10:16.925 --> 10:18.958
I was playing a joke.

10:18.960 --> 10:20.226
Oh.

10:20.228 --> 10:22.061
It was funny.

10:23.564 --> 10:25.798
Oh... oh...

10:25.800 --> 10:27.800
Don't worry, little ro-buddy.

10:27.802 --> 10:29.969
We'll get you on life support.

10:29.971 --> 10:33.139
Or tech support.&lt;br/>Oh, he would've loved that joke.

10:33.141 --> 10:35.708
I lost the head&lt;br/>of one of my toys once.

10:35.710 --> 10:39.345
Of course, I had to go to the&lt;br/>emergency room to get it out.

10:40.681 --> 10:44.183
Um, listen, I know this&lt;br/>may not be an opportune moment,

10:44.185 --> 10:48.421
but, um, I was wondering,&lt;br/>would you do me the honor of...

10:48.423 --> 10:49.722
being my best man?

10:49.724 --> 10:52.792
Of course. I would have&lt;br/>been hurt if you didn't ask.

10:52.794 --> 10:54.027
Oh, thanks, thanks. Great, man.

10:54.029 --> 10:55.762
Uh, oh, and better get&lt;br/>your speech ready

10:55.764 --> 10:56.863
for the rehearsal dinner.

10:56.865 --> 10:58.398
I'm taking everybody&lt;br/>to Souplantation.

10:58.400 --> 11:00.266
Fingers crossed we all end up&lt;br/>at the same table.

11:00.268 --> 11:01.901
Come on, come on,&lt;br/>come on. We...

11:01.903 --> 11:03.036
we got to go someplace fancier.

11:03.038 --> 11:05.104
Well, I would love to,&lt;br/>but I can't affo...

11:05.106 --> 11:06.005
I'll pay for it.

11:06.007 --> 11:07.006
Great. We've got reservations

11:07.008 --> 11:08.341
at 7:30 at La Dolce.

11:09.076 --> 11:11.077
♪ &lt;i>Men.&lt;/i> ♪

11:13.381 --> 11:16.349
I would like to make a toast&lt;br/>to the bride and groom.

11:16.351 --> 11:19.352
Um, I don't&lt;br/>look at this

11:19.354 --> 11:21.320
as losing a friend

11:21.322 --> 11:24.090
so much as gaining a guest room.

11:25.393 --> 11:28.461
I don't see this as&lt;br/>losing a friend either.

11:30.130 --> 11:32.432
Anyway, uh, to the happy couple.

11:32.434 --> 11:33.699
Uh, Alan,

11:33.701 --> 11:35.701
you're like a brother to me.

11:35.703 --> 11:38.204
And, Gretchen,&lt;br/>you...

11:38.206 --> 11:42.442
have a smile that lights up&lt;br/>those around you

11:42.444 --> 11:45.478
and a heart big enough&lt;br/>to let them all in.

11:45.480 --> 11:46.612
So...

11:46.614 --> 11:48.081
cheers.

11:48.083 --> 11:50.483
That was so sweet.

11:50.485 --> 11:51.984
Is he gay?

11:51.986 --> 11:55.188
If he was, you think&lt;br/>I'd be with you right now?

11:55.889 --> 11:57.657
♪ &lt;i>Men.&lt;/i> ♪

11:59.327 --> 12:00.760
Um, occupied.

12:02.130 --> 12:04.497
&lt;i>Ocupado.&lt;/i>

12:06.234 --> 12:09.569
&lt;i>S-Sprechen Sie&lt;/i> poopin.

12:09.571 --> 12:11.437
Alan.

12:11.439 --> 12:13.272
Lyndsey?!

12:13.274 --> 12:14.574
I need to talk to you.

12:14.576 --> 12:17.276
You scared the crap out of me.&lt;br/>Literally.

12:17.278 --> 12:18.578
This'll just take a sec.

12:18.580 --> 12:19.712
Wh-What are you doing?

12:19.714 --> 12:21.647
My whole family's here&lt;br/>in the restaurant.

12:21.649 --> 12:24.283
I'm here to say yes.

12:24.285 --> 12:25.818
To what?

12:25.820 --> 12:27.854
Your proposal.

12:27.856 --> 12:29.222
I want to be your wife.

12:29.224 --> 12:32.492
I am yours forever&lt;br/>and ever and ever.

12:32.494 --> 12:35.194
I am crazy for you.

12:35.196 --> 12:37.663
Oh, I don't doubt that.

12:37.665 --> 12:39.098
You know you still want me.

12:39.100 --> 12:40.867
Fate has brought us here&lt;br/>together.

12:40.869 --> 12:42.935
Uh, actually,&lt;br/>my lactose intolerance

12:42.937 --> 12:45.271
has brought us here together.

12:45.273 --> 12:48.174
Whatever. It was meant to be.

12:48.176 --> 12:49.408
Um, Lyndsey, Lyndsey,

12:49.410 --> 12:51.911
a-as romantic as this moment is,

12:51.913 --> 12:55.448
um, uh, I-I'm in love&lt;br/>with Gretchen.

12:56.216 --> 13:00.319
What happened to me?

13:00.321 --> 13:02.288
I was the prize.

13:02.290 --> 13:05.291
Men were fighting over me.

13:05.293 --> 13:09.295
Am I not hot anymore?

13:11.266 --> 13:13.499
Oh, I'm gonna need that.

13:16.570 --> 13:18.237
Here.

13:18.239 --> 13:21.507
They're sanitized&lt;br/>for your protection.

13:23.144 --> 13:25.144
Look, I-I still care&lt;br/>about you and...

13:25.146 --> 13:26.846
Oh, stop it.

13:26.848 --> 13:29.081
I don't want your pity.

13:29.083 --> 13:33.019
I'm gonna get out of here&lt;br/>while I still have my dignity.

13:38.892 --> 13:40.359
Oh, great.

13:40.361 --> 13:43.663
Now everyone at the table's&lt;br/>gonna know I was pooping.

13:43.665 --> 13:47.133
♪ &lt;i>Men.&lt;/i> ♪

13:47.135 --> 13:48.734
Hey, Alan,

13:48.736 --> 13:51.537
I have a little surprise&lt;br/>for your big day.

13:51.539 --> 13:53.573
Oh! Cash or check?

13:53.575 --> 13:55.775
I brought Jake to the wedding.

13:55.777 --> 13:57.710
My son. Yes. Yes.

13:57.712 --> 13:59.779
Yes, that's-that's way better&lt;br/>than cash.

13:59.781 --> 14:02.615
Um, uh, where is he?

14:02.617 --> 14:05.318
Hi, Dad.

14:05.320 --> 14:07.420
Pull my finger.

14:11.225 --> 14:14.260
Classic Robot Jake.

14:14.262 --> 14:15.962
Alan, can I see you a second?

14:15.964 --> 14:17.597
Oh, did you see Jake came&lt;br/>to the wedding?

14:17.599 --> 14:20.700
Sure, of course. Hello, Jake.

14:25.906 --> 14:27.907
Hey, Larry.

14:27.909 --> 14:29.508
Hey.

14:29.510 --> 14:31.911
You're looking...&lt;br/>pretty pensive.

14:31.913 --> 14:35.047
Oh, thanks, it's a rental.

14:35.049 --> 14:38.351
You look pretty&lt;br/>pensive, too.

14:38.353 --> 14:40.286
Actually...

14:40.288 --> 14:42.154
Thank you.

14:42.156 --> 14:46.592
Uh, hey, I just wanted&lt;br/>to say that it's, um....

14:46.594 --> 14:48.894
it's pretty big of you&lt;br/>to forgive Alan the way you did.

14:48.896 --> 14:50.830
I mean,

14:50.832 --> 14:53.165
after hearing that he was&lt;br/>still sleeping with Lyndsey

14:53.167 --> 14:55.201
when you two&lt;br/>were dating...

14:56.069 --> 14:58.738
...is apparently something&lt;br/>you're hearing

14:58.740 --> 15:00.673
for the first time&lt;br/>right now.

15:00.675 --> 15:02.675
Are you freakin' kidding me?&lt;br/>They were cheating?!

15:02.677 --> 15:03.809
I'll kill him!

15:03.811 --> 15:04.944
Larry, Larry,

15:04.946 --> 15:06.879
I'm sorry.&lt;br/>For what?

15:06.881 --> 15:09.081
This.

15:13.320 --> 15:15.788
Okay, let's get this show&lt;br/>on the road!

15:15.790 --> 15:17.990
Whoa, whoa, whoa.&lt;br/>What-What's the rush?

15:17.992 --> 15:19.759
Oh, uh,&lt;br/>I accidentally told Larry

15:19.761 --> 15:21.661
that you and Lyndsey&lt;br/>were cheating on him,

15:21.663 --> 15:24.397
so he wanted to kill you&lt;br/>so I pushed him off the deck.

15:24.399 --> 15:26.399
Let's go! Showtime!&lt;br/>Chop, chop! Come on!

15:30.971 --> 15:32.571
Oh,

15:32.573 --> 15:35.641
wow, so pensive.

15:36.677 --> 15:37.910
Where's my brother?

15:37.912 --> 15:39.145
Oh.

15:39.147 --> 15:40.212
Uh,

15:40.214 --> 15:43.015
he was overcome with emotion.

15:43.017 --> 15:45.818
So he hit the beach.

15:46.820 --> 15:47.953
Uh, but don't worry.&lt;br/>I'm filming it.

15:47.955 --> 15:49.822
Oh, by the way,&lt;br/>if you trip on your dress

15:49.824 --> 15:53.359
and accidentally flash us,&lt;br/>just go with it.

15:55.062 --> 15:56.395
A-All right, honey,&lt;br/>you look beautiful,

15:56.397 --> 15:57.697
but let's move it along, please.

15:58.965 --> 16:01.934
Uh, Jenny, hit it.

16:01.936 --> 16:04.603
"Daughters, mothers, sisters,&lt;br/>we gather here,

16:04.605 --> 16:07.940
safe from the patriarchy and the&lt;br/>oppression of its penises..."

16:07.942 --> 16:09.709
Oh, I really should've&lt;br/>revised this

16:09.711 --> 16:11.177
before doing a straight wedding.

16:11.179 --> 16:14.714
Um, wh-why don't we, uh, skip&lt;br/>to the vows that you guys wrote?

16:14.716 --> 16:16.849
All right. Um...

16:16.851 --> 16:21.487
I, Gretchen, do swear&lt;br/>to honor and cherish you.

16:21.489 --> 16:24.323
You asked me to go down&lt;br/>the road of life with you,

16:24.325 --> 16:25.891
and I am answering.

16:25.893 --> 16:28.027
I will go down.

16:28.029 --> 16:31.330
That's what she said.

16:31.332 --> 16:33.966
And I, Alan, do swear to honor,

16:33.968 --> 16:36.001
cherish and stand behind you

16:36.003 --> 16:37.570
whether things are easy

16:37.572 --> 16:39.171
or things are hard.

16:39.173 --> 16:42.174
That's what he said.

16:42.176 --> 16:44.243
Alan, do you take Gretchen&lt;br/>to be your...

16:44.245 --> 16:45.778
I object!

16:48.081 --> 16:49.081
Lyndsey?

16:51.485 --> 16:53.085
Lyndsey, Lyndsey,&lt;br/>you can't be here.

16:53.087 --> 16:54.987
Aren't I a pretty, pretty bride,&lt;br/>Alan?

16:54.989 --> 16:56.489
Yes.

16:56.491 --> 16:58.824
You look insanely&lt;br/>beautiful.

16:58.826 --> 16:59.892
Uh, now let's&lt;br/>turn you around

16:59.894 --> 17:01.427
and get you in a&lt;br/>cab. How 'bout...

17:01.429 --> 17:03.496
No!

17:04.164 --> 17:06.632
This was supposed to be my day!

17:06.634 --> 17:07.967
My wedding!

17:07.969 --> 17:09.969
My groom!

17:09.971 --> 17:12.571
My f... Wait.

17:12.573 --> 17:14.440
Those are my flowers.

17:14.442 --> 17:18.277
That's my food!

17:18.279 --> 17:20.913
Those are my linens.

17:20.915 --> 17:24.683
That's my...

17:24.685 --> 17:27.453
I think&lt;br/>she was gonna say "cake"!

17:31.958 --> 17:34.593
I always liked her.

17:34.595 --> 17:37.596
So, uh...&lt;br/>so where were we?

17:37.598 --> 17:39.165
Gretchen?

17:39.167 --> 17:40.466
Derek?

17:40.468 --> 17:41.333
Who's this guy?

17:42.669 --> 17:43.936
He's my ex-husband.

17:43.938 --> 17:46.539
Oh, come on!

17:46.541 --> 17:48.274
What are you doing here?

17:48.276 --> 17:51.777
Some crazy lady called and said&lt;br/>you were getting married.

17:51.779 --> 17:52.878
Well,&lt;br/>actually,

17:52.880 --> 17:54.113
what she said was,

17:54.115 --> 17:55.915
"Gretchen, pretty, pretty brid""

17:55.917 --> 17:59.151
followed by two minutes&lt;br/>of intense vomiting.

17:59.153 --> 18:00.786
Pretty sure&lt;br/>that was her.

18:00.788 --> 18:03.889
Boo-ya!

18:03.891 --> 18:05.558
Gretchen, I know I made&lt;br/>some horrible mistakes.

18:05.560 --> 18:07.393
I drank too much,&lt;br/>I wrecked your truck,

18:07.395 --> 18:09.728
I cheated on you&lt;br/>with your best friend.

18:09.730 --> 18:11.664
In your truck.&lt;br/>While I was drunk.

18:11.666 --> 18:13.132
Which is why&lt;br/>I wrecked it.

18:13.134 --> 18:15.367
Lose your dog&lt;br/>and you got a country song.

18:15.369 --> 18:17.903
I wouldn't know.&lt;br/>I'm more into hip-hop.

18:17.905 --> 18:20.239
I miss you, baby.&lt;br/>I want you back.

18:20.241 --> 18:21.340
Hey, Derek,

18:21.342 --> 18:22.408
if you want her back,

18:22.410 --> 18:24.310
you're gonna have&lt;br/>to go through me.

18:24.312 --> 18:25.544
Fine by me.

18:25.546 --> 18:27.213
And him.

18:27.215 --> 18:30.082
Look, seeing you in that&lt;br/>white dress right before

18:30.084 --> 18:32.985
I beat up two goobers&lt;br/>reminds me of our wedding.

18:32.987 --> 18:35.454
But this time the cake's not&lt;br/>in the shape of Dale Jr.,

18:35.456 --> 18:37.423
which is a&lt;br/>huge oversight.

18:39.359 --> 18:41.460
Derek...

18:41.462 --> 18:43.496
You're not actually&lt;br/>considering this, are you?

18:43.498 --> 18:44.864
I don't know. I'm so confused.

18:44.866 --> 18:47.233
I mean, Derek and I have&lt;br/>so much history together.

18:47.235 --> 18:49.201
This is really hard.

18:49.203 --> 18:50.402
That's what she said.

18:52.707 --> 18:55.474
That's what they say.

18:55.476 --> 18:59.011
I'm sorry, Alan. I-I at least&lt;br/>have to talk to him.

19:00.447 --> 19:01.580
Gretchen, wait!

19:01.582 --> 19:04.250
It's times like this&lt;br/>a son needs his mother.

19:04.252 --> 19:06.685
I'm gonna slip out&lt;br/>the back.

19:06.687 --> 19:09.555
Serves you right,&lt;br/>you bastard.

19:09.557 --> 19:11.557
I mean, I love you.

19:11.559 --> 19:15.394
Let's work this out.

19:15.396 --> 19:17.663
Best wedding ever!

19:17.665 --> 19:20.065
Yep! And I got&lt;br/>the whole thing on...

19:20.067 --> 19:23.869
Aw, crap, I had it on photo.

19:24.604 --> 19:26.972
♪ &lt;i>Men.&lt;/i> ♪

19:30.219 --> 19:31.920
How you doing?

19:31.922 --> 19:34.089
I've had better days.

19:34.091 --> 19:36.758
Hey, I'm sorry, buddy.

19:36.760 --> 19:40.061
Later, I'll run&lt;br/>you a Bublé bath.

19:40.063 --> 19:42.731
Thanks.

19:42.733 --> 19:44.399
Gretchen called.

19:44.401 --> 19:46.034
She said it's not over.

19:46.036 --> 19:48.270
She's just sorting things out.

19:48.272 --> 19:50.338
Oh, buddy.

19:51.340 --> 19:53.475
"Sorting things out"&lt;br/>is just people's way

19:53.477 --> 19:56.111
of not giving you bad news.

19:57.747 --> 19:59.548
So I take it your...

19:59.550 --> 20:03.618
mom's not gonna give you the&lt;br/>money for your own place?

20:04.453 --> 20:07.622
I'm just sorting&lt;br/>things out.

20:07.624 --> 20:09.958
You know what?

20:09.960 --> 20:12.494
I didn't really want&lt;br/>you to leave anyway.

20:12.496 --> 20:14.696
Aw. Thanks.

20:15.765 --> 20:17.699
Can you believe it?

20:17.701 --> 20:20.936
We're still together,&lt;br/>three years later.

20:20.938 --> 20:22.404
I know.

20:22.406 --> 20:25.907
I thought for sure&lt;br/>it was over when Charlie died.

20:25.909 --> 20:28.109
Thank God I showed up.

20:30.980 --> 20:33.248
You're telling me.&lt;br/>Hmm.

20:33.250 --> 20:35.250
I... You know,&lt;br/>I've been so busy lately.

20:35.252 --> 20:36.885
I-I really miss&lt;br/>hanging out with you.

20:36.887 --> 20:39.487
Yeah. Me, too. You know,&lt;br/>we should pick a night

20:39.489 --> 20:41.790
where we just&lt;br/>always get together.

20:41.792 --> 20:45.126
No matter what's going on,&lt;br/>once a week, we just do this.

20:45.128 --> 20:46.895
Okay, I like it.&lt;br/>I like it.

20:46.897 --> 20:49.264
How 'bout, uh, here&lt;br/>every Thursday night?

20:49.266 --> 20:50.432
9:00.

20:50.434 --> 20:51.233
It's a date.

20:51.235 --> 20:52.868
Uh, don't call it a date.

20:52.870 --> 20:55.537
Just call it...&lt;br/>two men hanging out.

20:55.539 --> 20:57.172
Hey.

20:57.174 --> 20:59.040
What about me?

20:59.042 --> 21:01.543
Okay, fine.&lt;br/>Two and a half men.

21:01.545 --> 21:06.545
== sync, corrected by &lt;font color=#00FF00>elderman&lt;/font> ==&lt;br/>&lt;font color=#00FFFF>@elder_man&lt;/font>
